  "answer_text": "Here is a complete overview of the MLA and MP seats in Telangana:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f MLA Seats (State Legislative Assembly)\n\nThe Legislative Assembly of Telangana currently consists of **119 elected members (MLAs)**.\n\n- The Telangana Legislative Assembly came into existence with 119 seats in **June 2014** with the formation of Telangana.\n- The members of the Vidhan Sabha are directly elected by the people through adult franchise.\n- The Legislature is **bicameral**, with **119 members of the Legislative Assembly** and **40 members of the Legislative Council**.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f MP Seats (Parliament)\n\n### Lok Sabha (Lower House):\nThe Lok Sabha of Telangana has **17 seats**.\n\nThe 17 Lok Sabha constituencies in Telangana are:\nAdilabad, Bhongir, Chevella, Hyderabad, Karimnagar, Khammam, Mahabubabad, Mahabubnagar, Malkajgiri, Medak, Nagarkurnool, Nalgonda, Nizamabad, Peddapalli, Secunderabad, Warangal, and Zahirabad.\n\n### Rajya Sabha (Upper House):\nTelangana has **7 seats** in the Rajya Sabha.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcca Summary Table\n\n| House | Seats |\n|---|---|\n| Legislative Assembly (MLA) | **119** |\n| Legislative Council (MLC) | **40** |\n| Lok Sabha (MP - Lower House) | **17** |\n| Rajya Sabha (MP - Upper House) | **7** |",
